<item><title>Mauritania hosts West African Quran memorization contest</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/mr/mauritania-hosts-west-african-quran-memorization-contest-dd5823/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/mr/mauritania-hosts-west-african-quran-memorization-contest-dd5823/</guid><category>Mauritania</category><description>Over 160 participants from 16 West African nations are competing in Nouakchott in the second edition of a Saudi-sponsored competition focused on the Quran and Sunna.</description><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:13:36 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/mr.jpg" length="34560" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/mr.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Mauritania orders EU fishing vessels to leave its waters</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/mr/mauritania-orders-eu-fishing-vessels-to-leave-its-waters-86934c/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/mr/mauritania-orders-eu-fishing-vessels-to-leave-its-waters-86934c/</guid><category>Mauritania</category><description>Mauritania&apos;s coast guard has told European Union fishing boats to head to the port of Nouadhibou before the fishing protocol expires at midnight.</description><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:36:25 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/mr/mauritania-orders-eu-fishing-vessels-to-leave-its-waters-86934c/share.jpg" length="40144" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/mr/mauritania-orders-eu-fishing-vessels-to-leave-its-waters-86934c/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
